# Xcode
build/
DerivedData/
*.xcuserstate
xcuserdata/
*.xcscmblueprint
*.xccheckout
*.moved-aside

# The .xcodeproj is committed on purpose so the repo opens with no tooling
# installed (see docs/TECH.md), but per-user state inside it is not.
*.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
*.xcodeproj/xcuserdata/

# Swift Package Manager
.build/
.swiftpm/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Per-user agent permissions. WORKFLOW.md is shared on purpose; this is not —
# it is one machine's allowlist, and it is the kind of file a `git add -A`
# sweeps in without anyone deciding to.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Per-machine signing (team id). See Config/Signing.xcconfig.
Config/Local.xcconfig

# Task briefs handed to agent sessions. Per-task scratch, not project history —
# the reasoning that matters ends up in the commit message instead.
.claude/briefs/
.claude/WORKFLOW.md

# Measurement artefacts. Screenshots, recordings and captures are how sessions
# verify UI work, and they keep wanting to land next to the document that cites
# them — 1.2 MB of accent comparisons had to be purged from history once
# already. The numbers belong in the repo; the pictures belong on the machine
# that took them.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.mov
*.mp4
*.xcresult/
docs/accent/
!BoringTracker/**/*.png
!**/Assets.xcassets/**/*.png
